# syncintosh architecture

The full canon is in `AGENTS.md`. This rule is the **always-on** part.

## Layers (dependencies point one way, inward)

```
cli/ ──▶ services/ ──▶ core/                    (core is pure, stdlib only)
adapters/ · presets/ · crypto/ · vcs/ · system/ · llm/ ──▶ core/   (infrastructure)
```

```
src/syncintosh/
├── cli/          Typer entrypoints + Rich rendering — wiring only, no logic
├── core/         Pure domain: models, manifest, merge engine, conflicts, ports
├── services/     Use-cases: collect · diff · merge · apply · sync · resolve · key-rotate
├── adapters/     Format adapters: jsonc · toml · yaml · xml · plist · text · binary
├── presets/      Built-in preset catalog (paths, noise, bundle IDs, URLs, casks)
├── crypto/       AES-256-GCM envelope, HKDF, manifest encryption, key wrapping, keyring
├── vcs/          git CLI subprocess transport
├── system/       Collection, app detection, launchd, watchdog, secret scan
└── llm/          OpenAI-compatible client, masking, validation
```

## Absolute rules

1. **`core` is pure** — stdlib only, no I/O, no third-party, no `subprocess`, no clock or
   env reads. Anything external needs a port in `core/ports.py`.
2. **Ports in `core`, implementations in infrastructure.** `core`/`services` never name a
   concrete adapter/crypto/vcs class.
3. **`cli` holds no logic** — parse, call a service, render.
4. **Collection copies, never symlinks** — IDEs' atomic saves sever symlinks.
5. **Adapters round-trip** — comments, key order, and formatting preserved.
6. **No I/O in constructors** — use explicit factories.
7. **Frozen boundary models** — no `obj.x = ...` after construction.
8. **State-changing ops return `None`, raise on failure.**

## Security invariants (the most dangerous)

- Ciphertext envelope is `version(1B) | nonce(12B) | ciphertext | tag(16B)`. **Layout fixed.**
- **AAD = file ID + format version** on both encrypt and decrypt.
- Nonce is random per encryption; never a counter, never reused.
- Stable random file ID → `objects/<id>.enc`; the encrypted manifest holds the real path.
  Never encrypt the path into the filename.
- Plaintext lives only in `~/.local/share/syncintosh/work/`, outside git, git-ignored.
- Docker `auths` and TLS certs are **stripped in code**; dangerous paths blocked before collection.
- LLM: mask secrets/domains, validate output, propose → approve, backup commit before apply.
- Only URLs hard-coded in built-in presets are trusted.

## Commands

`uv` only (`pip`/bare `python` forbidden):

```bash
uv run ruff format && uv run ruff check --fix && uv run ty check && uv run pytest
```

All four must pass.
